Condition : 8 - Prior to the commencement of a Development Phase (including enabling and site preparation works), a Construction Travel Plan shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The Construction Travel Plan shall follow the current 'Travel Plan Development Control Guidance' issued by TfL and shall include: 

i) Targets for sustainable travel arrangements; 

ii) Effective measures for the on-going monitoring of the Plan; 

iii) A commitment to delivering the Plan objectives for the full construction period; 

iv) Effective mechanisms to achieve the objectives of the Plan by the construction workforce. e) A strategy for the ongoing monitoring and review of the travel plan. The measures in the approved plan shall be implemented for the duration of construction period. 

The Construction Travel Plan shall be implemented as approved. 

Reason: Due to the length of development which would require promoting a shift towards sustainable modes of transport for construction related activities and prevent adverse impacts on the highway network in accordance with Policies LP14 & LP51 of the Wandsworth Local Plan 2023-2038 (adopted July 2023), Policies T2, T3, T4 & T5 of the London Plan (2021), and Paragraphs 115, 116 & 117 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024).

Condition : 21 - Notwithstanding the details shown on the approved plans and set out in the supporting information, Landscape and Ecological Enhancement and Management Plans shall be�submitted�to and approved in writing by the local planning authority prior to the commencement of any above ground works. The Plan shall include details of all measures to provide biodiversity gain, including but not limited to: 

i) details of all proposed planting including species and plans, with priority given to wildlife friendly planting; 

ii) details of biodiverse roofs (including Biosolar�roofs), including details of extensive substrate base, seeding/plug planting, with priority given to native wildflower species and if possible features to be included within the substrate e.g. rope coils, sand, gravel, etc. (in accordance with The Gro Green Roof Code 2021); 

iii) orientation, target species and location for at least 4x bird boxes/bricks and 2x bat boxes/ bricks; 

iv) if lighting is required, a bat sensitive post-construction lighting plan to ensure that any lighting would be of a specification that minimises its impacts on bats and onsite habitats, in accordance with the BCT and ILP 2023 Guidance Note (including having a colour temperature of <2700k, no uplighters and no light spill onto ecological enhancements or habitats). 

v) details on the management to be implemented post-construction, which shall include management responsibilities and maintenance schedules for all hard and soft landscaped areas as well as the above-mentioned measures to provide biodiversity enhancements.  

